---Information about a candidate running for elected office.
---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaCandidate
---@field party? string The full name of the party the candidate is a member of.
---@field sourceId? string Upstream identifier, if they use a string
---@field orderOnBallot? string The order the candidate appears on the ballot for this contest.
---@field isIncumbent? boolean Whether the candidate is an incumbent (i.e., currently holds the same office this contest elects). If absent, this was unspecified in the source data.
---@field profession? string The candidate's profession (e.g. businessman, lawyer), presumably pre-politics.
---@field mid? string MID of candidate in knowledge graph, when available.
---@field unofficiallySourcedField? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList A list of proto fields that came from unofficial sources This is not surfaced back in the API. We will use this to trim out the response if only official data is requested.
---@field email? string The email address for the candidate's campaign.
---@field searchImageUrl? string A URL for a photo of the candidate, to be used only with Search.
---@field phone? string The voice phone number for the candidate's campaign office.
---@field photoUrl? string A URL for a photo of the candidate.
---@field kgForeignKey? string Foreign key (e.g. object of /type/object/key predicate) for this candidate in KG, if available. Foreign keys for candidates are based on the candidate's identifier in the source dataset; right now, only BIP candidates get one, and the FKs take the form /authority/civics/bip_candidate/$ctcl_uuid.
---@field sortOrder? number The source-specified order of this candidate on the ballot for this contest.
---@field channels? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaChannelList A list of known (social) media channels for this candidate.
---@field candidateName? string This is always populated with the name of a single candidate, as opposed to the name field above that may be a concatenation of names in a ticket. In a joint ticket this field either refers to the name of the top ticket candidate or the name of the running mate.
---@field biography? string
---@field candidateUrl? string The URL for the candidate's campaign web site.
---@field runningMate? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaCandidate If the race is a joint ticket, this contains a pointer to the candidate's running mate.
---@field id? string
---@field personId? string Next ID: 23 A unique id from the connected Person object.
---@field name? string
---@field filedMailingAddress? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaSimpleAddressType The officially filed mailing address of the candidate.

