---Information about a contest that appears on a voter's ballot.
---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaContest
---@field generalElectionContestId? string The contest id for the general election. This is a vendor-specific identifier that doesn't correspond to a CIS identifier.
---@field referendumEffectOfAbstain? string Specifies what effect abstaining (not voting) on the proposition will have (i.e. whether abstaining is considered a vote against it). This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field contestMid? string The KG MID (type:/government/election) of this contest.
---@field referendumUrl? string A link to the referendum. This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field level_v1? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaContestLevel_v1Enum The level of office for this contest. One of: federal, state, county, city, other
---@field electionId? string
---@field datasetId? string
---@field referendumTopic? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaReferendumTopicList A list of topics of a referendum. This field is only populated for contests of the type 'Referendum'.
---@field isRetention? boolean
---@field numberElected? string The number of candidates that will be elected to office in this contest.
---@field district? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaElectoralDistrict Information about the electoral district that this contest is in.
---@field referendumSubtitle? string A brief description of the referendum. This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field numberVotingFor? string The number of candidates that a voter may vote for in this contest.
---@field officeBody? string The specific governmental body the office is a part of, including the jurisdiction.
---@field localizedOfficeDescription? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaLocalizedStringList Localized descriptions of the office this candidate is running for in 300 characters or less. The entries should be treated as a map. The same locale should not occur more than once.
---@field referendumPassageThreshold? string The threshold of votes that the referendum needs in order to pass, e.g. "two-thirds". This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field internal_id? string
---@field ballotTitle? string The official title on the ballot for this contest, only where available.
---@field level? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaContestLevelItemEnumList The levels of government of the office for this contest. There may be more than one in cases where a jurisdiction effectively acts at two different levels of government; for example, the mayor of the District of Columbia acts at "locality" level, but also effectively at both "administrative-area-2" and "administrative-area-1".
---@field type? string
---@field partisan? string This is basically never populated and is implied by the type being "Primary" in most cases. We'll add this back if it proves to be useful.
---@field officeCategory? string The category of the office. This should describe the governmental body w/o geographic identifiers. For example, the NC State Senate might be described as "State Senate". For now this is a string but we may deprecate it for an enumeration in the future.
---@field ballotPlacement? string A number specifying the position of this contest on the voter's ballot.
---@field ballot? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaBallot The candidates. The Ballot object is flattened in code to the Contest.candidate field when it is returned through the API so this field doesn't need to be exposed.
---@field officeDescription? string A description of the office this candidate is running for in 300 characters or less. The language is in the user's locale (obtained from the request). If the locale cannot be determined, an available English description is returned.
---@field referendumBallotResponses? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList The set of ballot responses for the referendum. A ballot response represents a line on the ballot. Common examples might include "yes" or "no" for referenda. This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field primaryParties? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList If this is a partisan election, the name of the party/parties it is for.
---@field jurisdiction? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaElectoralDistrict Information about the jurisdiction that this office has (as opposed to the set of voters that elect the office).
---@field startDate? string When does the winner take office? "yyyy-MM-dd"
---@field referendumTitle? string The title of the referendum (e.g. 'Proposition 42'). This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field candidates? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaCandidateList The candidate choices for this contest. This field is populated by a manual flattening in code of the Ballot.candidate field.
---@field referendumBrief? string Specifies a short summary of the referendum that is typically on the ballot below the title but above the text. This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field seat? string Extra disambiguating text for distinct seats within the same office (and district, where applicable).
---@field contestExt? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaContest
---@field roles? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaContestRolesItemEnumList The roles which this office fulfills.
---@field manuallyUpdated? boolean Indicates that the proto was manually updated and should not be overwritten by the pipeline.
---@field blocklisted? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaBlocklistEntry If this is not null, the contest has been blocklisted, and will never be returned in API responses.
---@field referendumText? string The full text of the referendum. This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field version? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaVersion
---@field office? string The name of the office for this contest.
---@field sources? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaSourceList A list of sources for this contest. If multiple sources are listed, the data has been aggregated from those sources.
---@field referendumConStatement? string A statement in opposition to the referendum. It does not necessarily appear on the ballot. This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field referendumProStatement? string A statement in favor of the referendum. It does not necessarily appear on the ballot. This field is only populated for contests of type 'Referendum'.
---@field electorateSpecifications? string A description of any additional eligibility requirements for voting in this contest.
---@field special? string "Yes" or "No" depending on whether this a contest being held outside the normal election cycle.

