---Describes the geographic scope of a contest.
---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaElectoralDistrict
---@field unverifiedOcdId? string An unverified OCD Division ID for this district. This could be an OCD ID we don't know about yet. We were unable to find it in our copy of the master repository.
---@field name? string
---@field scope? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaElectoralDistrictScopeEnum The geographic scope of this district. If unspecified the district's geography is not known. One of: national, statewide, congressional, stateUpper, stateLower, countywide, judicial, schoolBoard, cityWide, township, countyCouncil, cityCouncil, ward, special
---@field id? string An identifier for this district, relative to its scope. For example, the 34th State Senate district would have id "34" and a scope of stateUpper.
---@field feedId? string The id from the XML feed.
---@field ocdId? string The OCD Division ID for this district.
---@field kgForeignKey? string Foreign key (e.g. object of /type/object/key predicate) for this district in KG, if available. KG foreign keys for districts take the form /authority/civics/$canonical_ocd_id, with the specific exception that if the district is being used in the context of a Congressional election, the alias that has a /cd: component is preferred.
---@field state? string The state that this district is in. This is not returned in the API for now. This should be a lower case 2 digit abbreviation.

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaElectoralDistrictScopeEnum "statewide"|"congressional"|"stateUpper"|"stateLower"|"countywide"|"judicial"|"schoolBoard"|"citywide"|"special"|"countyCouncil"|"township"|"ward"|"cityCouncil"|"national"

---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlist
---@field entityDatasetId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList The dataset(s) to which this allowlist applies. If unset, applies to all datasets. Datasets control which entities are served, *not* which street segments are looked up. So you don't need to include the Targetsmart dataset ID to get voter-file-based objects. As a special case, 0 means "all positive-numbered datasets," to allow allowlisting all VIP data at once without having to worry about specific dataset IDs.
---@field pollingLocations? boolean Whether to serve election-day polling locations.
---@field regions? boolean Whether to serve regions.
---@field surfaceScope? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaSurfaceScope The surfaces to which this allowlist applies.
---@field contests? boolean Whether to serve contests. This is further restricted by contest_scopes if set.
---@field state? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList The US state(s) to which this allowlist applies. If unset, applies to all states.
---@field expectLowCoverage? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistExpectLowCoverageItemEnumList Entity types for expectation coverage. Does not affect what's served, but instructs our coverage monitoring to not alert for low coverage.
---@field contestScope? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistContestScopeItemEnumList Which scopes of contest to serve. If missing, and contests above is true, we will serve all contests
---@field earlyVote? boolean Whether to serve early-vote locations.
---@field dropOff? boolean Whether to serve drop-off locations.

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistContestScopeItemEnum "statewide"|"congressional"|"stateUpper"|"stateLower"|"countywide"|"judicial"|"schoolBoard"|"citywide"|"special"|"countyCouncil"|"township"|"ward"|"cityCouncil"|"national"

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistContestScopeItemEnumList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistContestScopeItemEnum[]

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistExpectLowCoverageItemEnum "entityTypeUnspecified"|"entityTypePollingLocation"|"entityTypeEarlyVote"|"entityTypeDropOff"|"entityTypeContest"|"entityTypeRegion"

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistExpectLowCoverageItemEnumList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistExpectLowCoverageItemEnum[]

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlistList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaEntityAllowlist[]

---Describes a political geography.
---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaGeographicDivision
---@field scope? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaGeographicDivisionScopeEnum The geographic scope of the division. If unspecified, the division's geography is not known. One of: national, statewide, congressional, stateUpper, stateLower, countywide, judicial, schoolBoard, cityWide, township, countyCouncil, cityCouncil, ward, special
---@field confidence? number Numerical value between 0 and 1 that expresses level of confidence that the location looked up is actually part of this district.
---@field alsoKnownAs? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList Any other valid OCD IDs that refer to the same division. Because OCD IDs are meant to be human-readable and at least somewhat predictable, there are occasionally several identifiers for a single division. These identifiers are defined to be equivalent to one another, and one is always indicated as the primary identifier. The primary identifier will be returned in ocd_id above, and any other equivalent valid identifiers will be returned in this list. For example, if this division's OCD ID is ocd-division/country:us/district:dc, this will contain ocd-division/country:us/state:dc.
---@field officeId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList Only present in query responses. List of keys in the offices object, one for each office elected from this division. Will only be present if includeOffices was true (or absent) in the request.
---@field geographicDivisionExt? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaGeographicDivision
---@field freebaseId? string The division's Freebase ID.
---@field ocdId? string The unique Open Civic Data identifier for this division.
---@field officeIndices? gcp.civicinfo_v2.IntegerList Only present in query responses. List of indices in the offices array, one for each office elected from this division. Will only be present if includeOffices was true (or absent) in the request.
---@field blocklisted? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaBlocklistEntry If this is present, the division has been blocklisted, and will never be returned in API responses.
---@field beforeManualUpdate? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaGeographicDivision If present, indicates that the proto was manually updated and should not be overwritten by the pipeline. This does *not* apply to any contained Offices, which track their own manual updates: it is possible for a GeographicDivision to be manually updated and not its contained Offices, or vice versa. This message contains the original contents from the pipeline, useful for comparing upstream data to our corrections. Any Offices from the original will be cleared.
---@field datasetId? string This field is used for indexing
---@field provenance? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StorageGraphBfgProvenance DEPRECATED We do not triplify feed data, so this should not be used. Provenance information about the data contained in this record, if available. Depending on the value of dataset_id, this may not be set.
---@field name? string The name of the division.
---@field office? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeList List of offices elected from this division. Only present in megastore.

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaGeographicDivisionMap { [string]: gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaGeographicDivision }

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaGeographicDivisionScopeEnum "statewide"|"congressional"|"stateUpper"|"stateLower"|"countywide"|"judicial"|"schoolBoard"|"citywide"|"special"|"countyCouncil"|"township"|"ward"|"cityCouncil"|"national"

