---Information about an Office held by one or more Officials.
---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOffice
---@field mapId? string A unique identifier for this office, within the context of this request. Identifiers are *not* long-lived: the same office may get different IDs on different requests.
---@field divisionId? string The OCD ID of the division with which this office is associated.
---@field freebaseId? string The office's Freebase ID.
---@field name? string
---@field levels? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeLevelsItemEnumList The levels of government of which this office is part. There may be more than one in cases where a jurisdiction effectively acts at two different levels of government; for example, the mayor of the District of Columbia acts at "locality" level, but also effectively at both "administrative-area-2" and "administrative-area-1".
---@field blocklisted? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaBlocklistEntry If this is present, the office has been blocklisted, and will never be returned in API responses.
---@field level? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeLevelEnum The level of this elected office. One of: federal, state, county, city, other
---@field official? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficialList A list of people who presently hold the office. Only present in megastore.
---@field roles? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeRolesItemEnumList The roles which this office fulfills. Roles are not meant to be exhaustive, or to exactly specify the entire set of responsibilities of a given office, but are meant to be rough categories that are useful for general selection from or sorting of a list of offices.
---@field officialId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList Only present in query responses. List of keys in the officials object of people who presently hold this office.
---@field id? string A unique identifier for this office.
---@field ocdId? string The office's Open Civic Data ID.
---@field sources? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaSourceList A list of sources for this office. If multiple sources are listed, the data has been aggregated from those sources.
---@field officialIndices? gcp.civicinfo_v2.IntegerList Only present in query responses. List of indices in the officials array of people who presently hold this office.
---@field beforeManualUpdate? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOffice If present, indicates that the proto was manually updated and should not be overwritten by the pipeline. This does *not* apply to any contained Officials, which track their own manual updates: it is possible for an Office to be manually updated and not its contained Officials, or vice versa. This message contains the original contents from the pipeline, useful for comparing upstream data to our corrections. Any Officials from the original will be cleared.

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeLevelEnum "federal"|"state"|"county"|"city"|"other"

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeLevelsItemEnum "international"|"country"|"administrativeArea1"|"regional"|"administrativeArea2"|"locality"|"subLocality1"|"subLocality2"|"special"

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeLevelsItemEnumList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeLevelsItemEnum[]

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOffice[]

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeRolesItemEnum "headOfState"|"headOfGovernment"|"deputyHeadOfGovernment"|"governmentOfficer"|"executiveCouncil"|"legislatorUpperBody"|"legislatorLowerBody"|"highestCourtJudge"|"judge"|"schoolBoard"|"specialPurposeOfficer"|"otherRole"

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeRolesItemEnumList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficeRolesItemEnum[]

---Information about a person holding an elected office.
---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficial
---@field phones? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList The official's public contact phone numbers.
---@field party? string The full name of the party the official belongs to.
---@field officialExt? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficial
---@field ocdId? string The official's Open Civic Data ID. This field is reserved in case the spec is completed.
---@field id? string A unique identifier for this official.
---@field channels? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaChannelList A list of known (social) media channels for this official.
---@field startDate? string Date when the officeholder first entered office in ISO format (yyyy-MM-dd) e.g. 2012-11-06
---@field name? string
---@field freebaseId? string The official's Freebase ID.
---@field urls? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList The official's public website URLs. This represents the verified version of the raw_urls field and will be populated only if raw URLs are successfully validated. Each URL will be be equal to its corresponding raw URL.
---@field blocklisted? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaBlocklistEntry If this is present, the official has been blocklisted, and will never be returned in API responses.
---@field geocodingSummaries? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoCommonGeocodingSummaryList Detailed summary about the official's address's geocoding
---@field emails? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList The direct email addresses for the official.
---@field beforeManualUpdate? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficial If present, indicates that the proto was manually updated and should not be overwritten by the pipeline. This message contains the original contents from the pipeline, useful for comparing upstream data to our corrections.
---@field rawAddresses? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList Raw, unnormalized addresses of the official taken directly from the source feed.
---@field photoUrl? string A URL for a photo of the official. This represents the verified version of the raw_photo_url field and will be populated only if the raw photo URL is successfully validated. This URL will be be equal to the raw photo URL.
---@field mapId? string A unique identifier for this official, within the context of this request. Identifiers are *not* long-lived: the same official may get different IDs on different requests.
---@field rawPhotoUrl? string A raw, unverified URL for a photo of the official, taken directly from the source feed.
---@field address? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaSimpleAddressTypeList Addresses at which to contact the official. This represents the normalized version of the raw_addresses field and will only be populated if raw addresses are successfully normalized by the geocoder.
---@field rawUrls? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList Raw, unverified URLs of the official's public websites, taken directly from the source feed.

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficialList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaOfficial[]

---Message that encapsulates polling hours.
---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingHours
---@field time? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaTimeIntervalList
---@field startDate? string Start date in ISO format (yyyy-MM-dd) e.g. 2012-11-06
---@field endDate? string Start date in ISO format (yyyy-MM-dd) e.g. 2012-11-06
---@field oba? boolean Or by appointment

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingHoursList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingHours[]

---A location where a voter can vote. This may be an early vote site, an election day voting location, or a drop off location for a completed ballot.
---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingLocation
---@field structuredPollingHours? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingHoursList Polling hours in structured form.
---@field voterProximityStats? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaVoterProximityStats Statistics about the proximity of the polling location and the street segments that map to it.
---@field isEarlyVoteSite? boolean These are additional fields related to the Early Vote Site objects. Surface in API as a separate list. No need to expose publicly. This is true if the location is an early vote location, regardless of whether it is also a drop off location.
---@field geocodedPoint? gcp.civicinfo_v2.GeostorePointProto Lat/Lng obtained from geocoding the polling location address.
---@field sources? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaSourceList A list of sources for this location. If multiple sources are listed the data has been aggregated from those sources.
---@field addressLine? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList The address of the polling location as a list of address lines. These come from the source data in VIP 5.0 and are geocoded to populate the structured address field above that is ultimately returned in the API.
---@field latitude? number Latitude of the location, in degrees north of the equator. Only some locations -- generally, ballot drop boxes for vote-by-mail elections -- will have this set; for others, use a geocoding service like the Google Maps API to resolve the address to a geographic point.
---@field name? string The name of the early vote site or drop off location. This field is not populated for polling locations.
---@field version? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaVersion
---@field geocodingValidationStatus? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingLocationGeocodingValidationStatusEnum Validation status of the geocoding for the polling location
---@field startDate? string The first date that this early vote site or drop off location may be used. This field is not populated for polling locations.
---@field notes? string Notes about this location (e.g. accessibility ramp or entrance to use).
---@field voterServices? string The services provided by this early vote site or drop off location. This field is not populated for polling locations.
---@field pollingHours? string A description of when this location is open.
---@field address? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaSimpleAddressType The address of the location.
---@field blocklisted? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaBlocklistEntry If this is not null, the polling location has been blocklisted, and will never be returned in API responses.
---@field endDate? string The last date that this early vote site or drop off location may be used. This field is not populated for polling locations.
---@field isDropOffLocation? boolean Is this site a ballot drop off location. This is true if the site is a ballot drop off location, regardless of whether it is also an early vote location.
---@field ocdId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList The OCD IDs for this polling location. Only used for unofficially sourced EV locations.
---@field longitude? number Longitude of the location, in degrees east of the Prime Meridian. Only some locations -- generally, ballot drop boxes for vote-by-mail elections -- will have this set; for others, use a geocoding service like the Google Maps API to resolve the address to a geographic point.
---@field internal_id? string
---@field geocodedOcdId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList OCD IDs for this polling location constructed from the geocoding result
---@field thirdPartyPoint? gcp.civicinfo_v2.GeostorePointProto Lat/Lng provided by the raw data source.
---@field electionId? string
---@field geocodingSummary? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoCommonGeocodingSummary Detailed summary about the polling location's geocoding
---@field startEndDatesAreRedundant? boolean Dates included in unstructured polling hours.
---@field datasetId? string
---@field manuallyUpdated? boolean Indicates that the proto was manually updated and should not be overwritten by the pipeline.
---@field providedLocationName? string The name of the polling location, as provided by the data provider.

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingLocationGeocodingValidationStatusEnum "unknown"|"noGeocodeFound"|"acceptedGeocoded"|"acceptedThirdParty"|"acceptedOptoolEdit"|"rejectedImpreciseFeature"|"rejectedVoterProximity"|"uncertainThirdParty"

---@alias gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingLocationList gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPollingLocation[]

---@class gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaPrecinct
---@field ward? string Specifies the ward the precinct is contained within.
---@field id? string Required. A unique identifier for this precinct.
---@field name? string Required. The name of the precinct.
---@field splitName? string If present, this proto corresponds to one portion of split precinct. Other portions of this precinct are guaranteed to have the same `name`. If not present, this proto represents a full precicnt.
---@field pollingLocationId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList ID(s) of the PollingLocation message(s) for this precinct.
---@field ocdId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList Encouraged. The OCD ID of the precinct
---@field spatialBoundaryId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList ID(s) of the SpatialBoundary message(s) for this precinct. Used to specify a geometrical boundary of the precinct.
---@field electoralDistrictId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList ID(s) of the ElectoralDistrict message(s) for this precinct.
---@field earlyVoteSiteId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList ID(s) of the PollingLocation message(s) for this precinct.
---@field datasetId? string Required. Dataset ID. What datasets our Precincts come from.
---@field contestId? gcp.civicinfo_v2.StringList ID(s) of the Contest message(s) for this precinct.
---@field administrationRegionId? string ID of the AdministrationRegion message for this precinct. Corresponds to LocalityId xml tag.
---@field version? gcp.civicinfo_v2.CivicinfoSchemaVersion Versioning metadata
---@field mailOnly? boolean Specifies if the precinct runs mail-only elections.
---@field number? string The number of the precinct.

